<!-- [WOLF TUNNELS 2026-10-22] The Tunnel tool (wolffloatertunnels.cpp). Paul: "make the tunneling work like the cave builder ...
     users should be able to 'Draw' the tunnel and it creates the mesh with caverns", and "offer smooth tunnels (like railways)
     or rough tunnels like someone would explore".
     [2026-10-22 simple] Paul still could not make one (wolfstorm/tools/TUNNEL_STRANGER_ASSESSMENT.md), and: "when I first show
     it, I just draw the tunnel, and it doesn't require me to create a new tunnel first."
     Persona: a region owner who has never built a tunnel and wants one through their hill in two minutes.
     Story: "I click where the tunnel goes in and where it comes out. It goes under the hill by itself, and I press Build."
     Flow: the window opens drawing (camera from above, pen on) -> 1. click In, bends, Out -> 2. what it is for (Path / Road /
     Railway) and its walls (Built / Natural) -> 3. Build tunnel -> Walk in. The hint line at the top says the next step; the
     line under Build says why it cannot be pressed, else the one note about the drawing. Expert (closed) holds the numbers; the
     region's tunnels (closed) hold Change, Walk in and Delete for tunnels built before.
     Layout: 464 high with both sections closed; Expert 260, its walkable boxes 250, the tunnels list 140 (heights must match
     WolfFloaterTunnels::relayout, which places the panels under each other). Build is in the part that is always shown.
     [WOLF BURROW 2026-10-23] Paul: "upgrade the whole tunnel floater please i LOVE the mole". The burrow look (wolfburrow.cpp):
     a painted header with the mole (20..64), each group on its own dark plate with an amber heading in the 20 px above its first
     row (and 22 px at the top of each panel), painted button faces (Build tunnel, Walk in and Light up amber; the rest stone;
     Delete, Start over and the box Delete with a red rule). Buttons draw no skin image (image_color 0 alpha); every text colour is
     fixed because it sits on the fixed paint (contrast: region-terrain-work/cave-lights/check/burrow_contrast.py). Same names,
     callbacks and behaviour. -->
